From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:48:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wineserver: read only the request fds of threads that have a
 request

The iOS server loop cannot poll its AF_UNIX client fds, so on every pass
it set a synthetic POLLIN on every client fd and tried a non-blocking
read() on each. With RDR2's 220-280 threads that was O(threads) failed
syscalls per pass: in run 20261020T081946-rdr2-r3 the wineserver thread
used 48-85 % of a core, almost all of it in read <- read_request <-
thread_poll_event <- main_loop. The wake semaphore made it worse: every
request signalled it and nothing drained it, so once requests (5-6 k/s)
outran the loop it stopped sleeping.

Server and clients are one process. A client now marks its thread id in
a shared set (wineserver/pp_srv_pending.h: a bitmap of ptids with a
summary word per 64 words) after it writes a request, and after it
closes its request fd as it ends. The loop drains the set each pass and
reads only those threads' request fds; the sweep still reads every
other client fd (process sockets) each pass, and the thread request fds
too on a full sweep every 50 ms, the net for a missed mark. An id the
set cannot hold (0 before init_first_thread's reply, or above 0xfffc)
asks for a full sweep at once. A partly read request is marked again;
a mark while the request fd waits for a reply's POLLOUT is retried
each pass.

The wake semaphore is signalled only by the first mark since the loop
last re-armed (once per pass, before it sleeps), and the loop does not
sleep while marks wait, so a mark is never left for the 1 ms tick and
the semaphore's count no longer grows with the request rate.

INET fds keep their real zero-timeout poll() each pass, and the loop
still wakes at least every 1 ms for timers, so Steam's CM pings keep
their budget. MADEIRA_SRV_PENDING=0 restores the old sweep for an A/B.
The heartbeat logs a [srv-pending] line: marks read, stale ids, partial
requests, deferred marks, full sweeps, forced ones, and requests a full
sweep found waiting (a missed mark, or one about to be made).

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-20-wineserver-pending-set.md
Offered-upstream: no; the in-process server loop is the iOS port's
